As I said, I don't know what dredge() is looking for, but the object produced by dsm is a 2-part object; part gam and part ddf object.  As described in documentation:

Value

a MailScanner has detected a possible fraud attempt from "127.0.0.1:38836" claiming to be glm <http://127.0.0.1:38836/help/library/dsm/help/glm>/MailScanner has detected a possible fraud attempt from "127.0.0.1:38836" claiming to be gam <http://127.0.0.1:38836/help/library/dsm/help/gam>/MailScanner has detected a possible fraud attempt from "127.0.0.1:38836" claiming to be gamm <http://127.0.0.1:38836/help/library/dsm/help/gamm> object, with an additional element, ddf which holds the detection function object.

Perhaps you need to tear off the gam part of the dsm object to pass to your magic function.

