Hi Len, thanks for the quick response. It turns out to be a problem due to a projection issue in the project. I was also having a problem generating a coverage layer and found a response from Laura explaining that Distance does not need to know about projections. Cleared away all the CRS information in a new project and re-projected from lat/long in QGIS. Now with the study area shapefile (in meters) loaded, the coverage layer is just as expected. This also apparently solved the effort allocation problem. It was not obvious that the two issues we were having were so closely related but there you are.

On a separate question, are you aware of anyone having used a scanning sonar to 'sight' schools of small pelagics in a distance sampling application? We have a sonar on the available research vessel but not the usual calibrated echosounder used for small pelagic fish surveys.

Regards,

Paul

